## 1. Objective

The `?mode=kiosk` path in `ic-client` currently shows delivery-type and payment-method toggles that make no sense on a walk-up terminal, collects phone + name + branch, and creates the order through the public `POST /api/create_order`, which pushes straight to the kitchen with **no payment taken**. This task ports the already-designed, already-shipping flow from the Expo/RN kiosk app (`Main/ic-pizza-kiosk`) into a **temporary web kiosk** inside `ic-client`, wired to the backend's `eazypay-integration` branch (already built, no backend changes in scope). Target flow: branch selector (exists) → new kiosk/terminal picker → cart with just a Checkout button → cross-sell (unchanged) → phone-only step → create order as `Pending Payment` → fire EazyPay at the terminal → poll and show "Tap your card" → **APPROVED** = backend settles and publishes to the kitchen itself → **any other terminal failure** = "pay at the front desk?" Yes/No → **No or 60s silence** = abandon the order, close everything, and clear the cart for the next customer.

## 2. Scope

**In scope:** everything named in the New files / Edits to existing files tables below, across the 8 phases. New `domains/kiosk/*` infrastructure (config, identity, branch resolution, triple-click re-pair gesture, payment polling, checkout state machine, session reset, 6 UI sheets), a new `shared/api/kiosk*` HTTP layer, a shared `orderPayload.ts` money/item-mapping extraction reused by both kiosk and non-kiosk checkout, a new `kiosk` i18n namespace, and the minimal edits to `useCheckout.ts`, `useMenuData.ts`, `HomePage.tsx`, `HomePageModals.tsx`, `HeroSection.tsx`, `CartComponent.tsx` needed to wire it in.

**Out of scope** (see §10 for the full list): any backend change, the non-kiosk `ClientInfoPopup` flow, the cross-sell logic itself (only its call-site gating), any refactor not explicitly named, a global idle timer for abandoned carts (explicitly deferred — see Risks), adding new npm dependencies, committing or pushing.

## 3. Non-negotiables (user-locked product decisions)

1. **No card retry.** Every terminal failure status (`DECLINED`/`CANCELLED`/`EXPIRED`/`ERROR`, plus the polling hook's own `TIMEOUT`) goes straight to the "pay at the front desk?" Yes/No sheet. `AMOUNT_MISMATCH` is the **one** exception — dead-ends to "see a member of staff", is **never** abandoned or deferred and gets **no** 60s timer, because money already left the card.
2. **Phone-only kiosk info step.** No name, no branch dropdown. `customer_name: null` on the payload. The non-kiosk `ClientInfoPopup` is **left completely untouched**.
3. **Re-pairing** = admin triple-clicks the **top of the hero video**. No PIN.
4. **All payment UI** is MUI `Drawer anchor="bottom"` bottom sheets, copying `src/domains/management/cash-register/components/CashInputDrawer.tsx` **exactly** (see §7). The user explicitly said "please pay attention to the UI" — this is a customer-facing walk-up screen.
5. **Nothing on the kiosk payment path may set `checkoutLoading`.** `HomePage.tsx:103` returns a full-page `<PizzaLoader/>` whenever `checkout.checkoutLoading` is true, which would unmount every sheet mid-payment.

## 4. System context

`ic-client` is a domain-first React 18 + CRA + MUI v7 app (`ic-client/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — architecture map). The customer-ordering flow is `HomePage.tsx` (thin shell) composing `useMenuData` → `useCart` → `useCheckout`, with all popups rendered by the sibling `HomePageModals.tsx`. Kiosk mode is detected via `isKioskSearch(searchParams)` (`shared/utils/kioskMode.ts`, `?mode=kiosk`) and today reuses the same `useCheckout`/`useMenuData` hooks with `isKiosk` branches sprinkled through them — this task **deletes** those inline branches and replaces them with a dedicated `domains/kiosk/*` module, following the existing domain-first convention (compare `domains/cart`, `domains/order`). The kiosk domain already has two files: `components/KioskBranchSelector.tsx` (the existing branch picker, kept and reused unchanged) and `components/ScrollHintArrow.tsx`. This task adds `services/`, `utils/`, `hooks/` and more `components/` under that same `domains/kiosk/` directory. All new HTTP calls follow the existing `shared/api/{client,public,management}.ts` pattern (one file per concern, manual Jest mocks in `shared/api/__mocks__/`) but get their **own** `kioskClient.ts`/`kiosk.ts` because kiosk devices carry no staff JWT and must never hit the `authFetch` 401→redirect path (`shared/api/client.ts:29-34`).

## 5. Backend contract (already built — READ ONLY, no backend changes in scope)

Branch `eazypay-integration` of `/Users/andrew/Documents/ICpizza/Main/backend` — **never checked out, never modified**; read with `git -C /Users/andrew/Documents/ICpizza/Main/backend show eazypay-integration:<path>`. All `/api/kiosk/**` routes require header `X-Kiosk-Name: <deviceName>` and send **no** bearer token; the backend returns 401 otherwise.

| Endpoint | Notes |
|---|---|
| `GET /kiosk/pairing/kiosks` | `permitAll`. Returns `[{deviceName, terminalId, branchId, branchName}]`. **Not branch-filtered by the backend** — the client filters by the branch already stored locally. |
| `POST /kiosk/orders` | Same body shape as `/api/create_order` (`CreateOrderRequest`). Creates the order with status `Pending Payment`, **not** pushed to the kitchen. The server overrides `payment_type`, `type`, and `branchId` regardless of what the client sends. `tel` is **required**. 409 → items unavailable (same `Items409Response` shape as `/api/create_order`), 423 → branch closed (`BranchClosedResponse`). |
| `POST /kiosk/payments/initiate` `{orderId}` | → `{invoiceNum, status}`. The device never sends an amount (the backend reads it off the order). **Idempotent per order** — calling it again for the same order is safe. |
| `GET /kiosk/payments/{invoiceNum}/result` | 16 fields including `cardNo`, `trnRrn`, `trnAuthCode`, `posEntryMode`, six `dcc*` fields, and `failureReason`. |
| `POST /kiosk/payments/{invoiceNum}/cancel` | Releases the terminal. |
| `POST /kiosk/orders/{id}/defer-to-counter` | Publishes the order, unpaid, to the kitchen as `Cash`. **Idempotent.** |
| `POST /kiosk/orders/{id}/abandon` | Hard-deletes the order. **Not idempotent** — a second call 404s. This is by design; do not "fix" it by retrying harder. |

`PaymentStatus` = `INITIATING | PENDING | APPROVED | DECLINED | CANCELLED | EXPIRED | AMOUNT_MISMATCH | ERROR`. Terminal states are all of these except `INITIATING`/`PENDING`. **On `APPROVED` the backend settles the payment and publishes the order to the kitchen itself — the client does nothing beyond showing confirmation and clearing the cart.**

