- `KioskPaymentFailureSheet`: 5 phases (`failed`/asking-yes-no, `deferred`-in-flight, `error-terminal`, `error-retryable`, the `mismatch` dead-end display), the 60s countdown in a **separate effect** from any tick/display effect, `expiredRef` capping the auto-abandon at one fire. Yes → `deferOrderToCounter` (409 → `error-terminal`; other → `error-retryable`, whose "Try again" re-invokes defer only). No → `abandonKioskOrder` (404 → treated as success). Silence → fire-and-forget abandon then reset.
- `KioskOrderApprovedSheet`: render the 6 `dcc*` fields only when `dccMsg ?? dccRate ?? dccAmount` is populated (§10).
- Sheets use `useTranslation(["kiosk", "checkout"])`; phone validation copy comes from `checkout`'s existing keys. `KioskTerminalPicker` stays English-only (plain strings or `enI18n`, matching `KioskBranchSelector`'s current plain-English copy).
- No `any`, no unexplained `as X`, explicit `Promise<T>` return types on every async handler.

**Acceptance criteria**
- `KioskPaymentFailureSheet.test.tsx`: all 5 phases render their distinct content; 409-on-defer routes to `error-terminal`; non-409-on-defer routes to `error-retryable`; 404-on-abandon is treated as success; the 60s timer fires abandon **exactly once** (fake timers, advance past 60s twice, assert one call).
- `KioskPhoneEntrySheet.test.tsx`: digits-only + length validation using the reused `checkout` i18n keys; an inline error does not clear already-typed digits; a spinner/disabled state shows while `submitting` is true.
- `KioskTerminalPicker.test.tsx`: client-side filtering of `fetchPairingOptions()` results by the locally-stored branch id; a selection persists via `kioskIdentity.setKioskDeviceName`; a `PairingUnavailableError` renders a diagnosable on-screen message (not a silent blank screen).
- `yarn tsc --noEmit` clean; full suite green.

