## 19. End-to-end verification (manual, once the backend branch is runnable)

1. `yarn tsc --noEmit` && `yarn test --watchAll=false` && `yarn build`. (`CI=true yarn build` failing on pre-existing project-wide ESLint warnings is not a regression signal.)
2. Backend: check out `eazypay-integration` (in the **backend** repo only — never in `ic-client`), apply the two manual DDL statements (unique index on `kiosks.device_name`; partial unique index on `payment_transactions(order_id) WHERE status IN ('INITIATING','PENDING')`), run with EazyPay credentials, register a kiosk via `POST /api/kiosk-admin/kiosks`.
3. `yarn start` → `http://localhost:3000/menu?mode=kiosk` — confirm this origin is on the backend's CORS allowlist (see the Open Question in §11). Pick branch → pick kiosk → add items → Checkout → cross-sell → Checkout → phone → "Tap your card".
4. Exercise all four terminal outcomes: approve; decline → Yes (order appears on the admin board unpaid as `Cash`); decline → No (order gone, cart cleared, back at the menu); decline → wait 60s (same end state as No).
5. Triple-click the top of the hero video → both pickers reopen.

