## 22. Open questions

These could not be resolved during this spec-writing pass because this environment had no shell/Bash tool (so `git -C backend show eazypay-integration:<path>` could not be run) and no filesystem read permission for `/Users/andrew/Documents/ICpizza/Main/backend` or `/Users/andrew/Documents/ICpizza/Main/ic-pizza-kiosk`. **Implementers of the affected phases must resolve these by reading the actual source before writing code that depends on them — do not guess.**

1. **Full `PaymentResultResponse` field list** (Phase 2) — only `cardNo`, `trnRrn`, `trnAuthCode`, `posEntryMode`, 3 of 6 `dcc*` field names, and `failureReason` are known from the plan text; the remaining ~9 of 16 fields (including the exact `dcc*` sextet) must be read off the backend DTO directly.
2. **`APPROVED_AUTO_RETURN_MS` numeric value** (Phase 1) — the plan names the constant but never gives a number; it must be copied from `ic-pizza-kiosk/services/config.ts`.
3. **`useTripleClick`'s default `windowMs`** — not specified anywhere in the plan or the RN reference description available to this pass; Phase 1's implementer should check `ic-pizza-kiosk`'s equivalent gesture (if one exists there) before picking an arbitrary value, and must document the chosen value with a comment either way.
4. **CORS allowlist currency** — the plan names `localhost:3000`, `ic-pizza.com`, `www.ic-pizza.com`, `icpizza-back.onrender.com`, but the actual `shared/api/client.ts` in this working tree points at `api.ic-pizza.com` (prod) / `localhost:8000` (dev), not `icpizza-back.onrender.com` / `:8080`. Confirm the real `eazypay-integration` backend's CORS allowlist against whatever origin `kioskFetch` actually targets before relying on it in manual testing (§19 step 3).
5. **Exact JSON field casing for the kiosk endpoints** (`invoiceNum` vs `invoice_num`, etc.) — assumed camelCase in §13 by analogy with the existing `Items409Response.unavailableIds` convention in this codebase, but not independently confirmed against the backend's serialization config for the `/kiosk/**` controllers specifically.

If any of the above cannot be resolved by reading the source directly (e.g. the backend branch truly isn't reachable), stop per the standing rule in §17 and write `needs-clarification.md` rather than inventing values.
